invariant: INV-16
file: sha512.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: on x86-64 sha512.h's sha512_on_instructions reads
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA512, arm64's bit, which every x86-64 init call
  refuses, so no session's value holds it and every SHA-384 and SHA-512
  call of an x86-64 session runs sha512_compress_blocks.c, whatever its
  caller states. The bytes are the same, so no vector can tell: the AVX2
  kernel is in the object and nothing runs it. bin/x86_kernels_test counts
  the compression calls each row sends to the kernel under every
  ch_cfg.cpu value and requires all of them there under CH_CPU_AVX2. Only
  an x86-64 object compiles this line of the predicate, so the catch is
  the script, which builds the binary for x86-64 and runs it under
  qemu-x86_64 on any host. The lane skips without docker, and this then
  reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX2) != 0;
--- new
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA512) != 0;
